\[\frac{x}{2}=13\cdot\frac1{2x}+60\frac x{2x}-60\frac {1}{2x}\cdot\frac {12}{x}=\frac{13}{x}+30-\frac {60}{x^2}.\]Moving everything to the left-hand side, we get

\[0=x^3-13x-30x^2+60=30x^2+30x+60=x(10x+10)+60.\]It follows that $x=5$.

Therefore, the least possible length, in units, of the third side is $\boxed{5}.$ </think> <answer> 5 </answer>

